subrahmaṇya. (M.B. śalya Parva, Chapter 45, Stanza 64).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomra", "dhoomra_2", "dhuumra", "dhuumra_2", "dhūmra", "dhūmra_2", "धूम्र", "ధూమ్ర", "ధూమ్ర_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರ", "ಧೂಮ್ರ_೨"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomra", "dhoomra_2", "dhuumra", "dhuumra_2", "dhūmra", "dhūmra_2", "DUmra", "ధూమ్ర", "ధూమ్ర_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರ", "ಧೂಮ್ರ_೨"]}], "Dumra": [{"id": "DUmrA", "headword": "धूम्रा", "headword_slp1": "DUmrA", "fold": "Dumra", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्रा\n\nDHŪMRĀ . A daughter of prajāpati dakṣa. She became the wife of Dharmadeva. Two sons, dhruva and dhara were born to the couple. (M.B. Ādi Parva, Chapter 66, Stanza 19).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomraa", "dhuumraa", "dhūmrā", "ధూమ్రా", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomraa", "dhuumraa", "dhūmrā", "ధూమ్రా", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾ"]}], "Dumrakesa_१": [{"id": "DUmrakeSa_१", "headword": "धूम्रकेश_१", "headword_slp1": "DUmrakeSa_१", "fold": "Dumrakesa_१", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्रकेश १\n\nDHŪMRAKEŚA I . A pracetas (bhāgavata, skandha 4).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomrakesha", "dhoomrakesha_1", "dhuumrakesha", "dhuumrakesha_1", "dhūmrakeśa", "dhūmrakeśa_1", "धूम्रकेश", "ధూమ్రకేశ", "ధూమ్రకేశ_౧", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ_೧"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomrakesha", "dhoomrakesha_1", "dhuumrakesha", "dhuumrakesha_1", "dhūmrakeśa", "dhūmrakeśa_1", "DUmrakeSa", "ధూమ్రకేశ", "ధూమ్రకేశ_౧", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ_೧"]}], "Dumrakesa_२": [{"id": "DUmrakeSa_२", "headword": "धूम्रकेश_२", "headword_slp1": "DUmrakeSa_२", "fold": "Dumrakesa_२", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्रकेश २\n\nDHŪMRAKEŚA II . The third son of pṛthu, the son of vena. Five sons were born to pṛthu by his wife arcis. On the death of pṛthu, his elder brother's son vijitāśva appointed dhūmrakeśa as the governor of southern countries. (bhāgavata, skandha 4).\n\nDHŪMRAKETU. A son of bharata. Five sons named sumati, Rāṣtrabhṛt, sudarśana, Varaṇa and Dhūmraketu were born to bharata by his wife pañcajanī. (bhāgavata, skandha 5).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomrakesha", "dhoomrakesha_2", "dhuumrakesha", "dhuumrakesha_2", "dhūmrakeśa", "dhūmrakeśa_2", "धूम्रकेश", "ధూమ్రకేశ", "ధూమ్రకేశ_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ_೨"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomrakesha", "dhoomrakesha_2", "dhuumrakesha", "dhuumrakesha_2", "dhūmrakeśa", "dhūmrakeśa_2", "DUmrakeSa", "ధూమ్రకేశ", "ధూమ్రకేశ_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಕೇಶ_೨"]}], "Dumraksa_१": [{"id": "DUmrAkza_१", "headword": "धूम्राक्ष_१", "headword_slp1": "DUmrAkza_१", "fold": "Dumraksa_१", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्राक्ष १\n\nDHŪMRĀKṢA I . A king of the ikṣvāku dynasty.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomraakSha", "dhoomraakSha_1", "dhuumraakSha", "dhuumraakSha_1", "dhuumraaxa", "dhuumraaxa_1", "dhūmrākṣa", "dhūmrākṣa_1", "धूम्राक्ष", "ధూమ్రాక్ష", "ధూమ్రాక్ష_౧", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ_೧"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomraakSha", "dhoomraakSha_1", "dhuumraakSha", "dhuumraakSha_1", "dhuumraaxa", "dhuumraaxa_1", "dhūmrākṣa", "dhūmrākṣa_1", "DUmrAkza", "ధూమ్రాక్ష", "ధూమ్రాక్ష_౧", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ_೧"]}], "Dumraksa_२": [{"id": "DUmrAkza_२", "headword": "धूम्राक्ष_२", "headword_slp1": "DUmrAkza_२", "fold": "Dumraksa_२", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्राक्ष २\n\nDHŪMRĀKṢA II . A minister of rāvaṇa. Genealogy. brahmā created the rākṣasa (giant) Heti. The son vidyutkeśa was born to him of his wife bhayā. sukeśa was born to vidyutkeśa by his wife sālakaṭaṅkā. sukeśa married devavatī. three sons, mālyavān, sumālī and mālī were born to the couple. To sumālī, by his wife ketumatī, fourteen children were born: prahasta, Akaṁpana, vikaṭa, kālakāmukha, dhūmrākṣa, daṇḍa, Supārśvā, saṁhrāda, Prākvāda, bhāsakarṇa, Veka, Puṣpotkaṭa, Kaikasi, and Kumbhīnasi; most of them were ministers of rāvaṇa. (uttara rāmāyaṇa).2) Work and death. dhūmrākṣa was one who worked in all the branches of administration of the state. In all the battles fought by the Rākṣasas dhūmrākṣa was present. He was also called Dhūmralocana. He was killed in the battle of rāma and rāvaṇa at the hands of hanūmān. (vālmīki rāmāyaṇa, yuddha Kāṇḍa, Chapter 51).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomraakSha", "dhoomraakSha_2", "dhuumraakSha", "dhuumraakSha_2", "dhuumraaxa", "dhuumraaxa_2", "dhūmrākṣa", "dhūmrākṣa_2", "धूम्राक्ष", "ధూమ్రాక్ష", "ధూమ్రాక్ష_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ_೨"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomraakSha", "dhoomraakSha_2", "dhuumraakSha", "dhuumraakSha_2", "dhuumraaxa", "dhuumraaxa_2", "dhūmrākṣa", "dhūmrākṣa_2", "DUmrAkza", "ధూమ్రాక్ష", "ధూమ్రాక్ష_౨", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಕ್ಷ_೨"]}], "Dumrasva": [{"id": "DUmrASva", "headword": "धूम्राश्व", "headword_slp1": "DUmrASva", "fold": "Dumrasva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "purana-encyclopedia", "senses": [{"gloss": "धूम्राश्व\n\nDHŪMRĀŚVA . A king of the ikṣvāku dynasty. He was the son of sucandra and the father of sañjaya. (vālmīki rāmāyaṇa, Bāla Kāṇḍa, sarga 47).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["dhoomraashva", "dhuumraashva", "dhūmrāśva", "ధూమ్రాశ్వ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಶ್ವ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dhoomraashva", "dhuumraashva", "dhūmrāśva", "ధూమ్రాశ్వ", "ಧೂಮ್ರಾಶ್ವ"]}]}